            "review_title": "Review at My Quang Ech Bep Trang",
            "review_text": "gramsay_22\nStromness, United Kingdom12 contributions\n0\nService non existent and mediocre food\nSep 2026 • Couples\nWe were initially really hopeful about this place. My partner and I seemed to be the only international tourists, and seeing how busy it was with local diners felt like a great sign — especially as it was our first time trying frog and we assumed this was somewhere people came specifically for the food.\nUnfortunately, the experience went downhill from there. Service was extremely poor, with our menus arriving around 15 minutes after we sat down and our food coming very slowly and separately. My partner had finished his meal before mine arrived, and we were even waiting longer than customers who had arrived and ordered the same dishes around 15 minutes after us. It was difficult not to feel that we were being overlooked because we were tourists.\n\nThe only reason we received any attention at all was thanks to a lovely Vietnamese family sitting next to us, who repeatedly advocated for us and asked the staff why we weren't being served. My Vietnamese is very basic, so I couldn't understand the explanations we were given.\n\nWe ordered the Mì Quảng Gà Chọi (fighting chicken) and Mì Quảng Ếch (frog). Sadly, both dishes were quite tasteless and didn't feel worth the effort it took to get them.\n\nIt's a real shame, as this was very different from the overwhelmingly warm and welcoming experiences we've had elsewhere in Vietnam.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten September 1, 2026",
